# lawpass_server environment — NOTE: config is CONSOLIDATED.
#
# There is NO separate server .env anymore. The server reads the SAME single
# file as the Next.js app: ../.env.local (i.e. app/.env.local). Copy the
# repo-root template `../.env.example` to `../.env.local` and fill it in once;
# it holds both the Next.js vars and the server vars (PORT, NODE_ENV,
# CORS_ORIGINS).
#
# config/env.js resolves the env file in this order (first that exists wins):
#   1. LAWPASS_ENV_PATH       — explicit path; in production point this at an
#                               env file kept OUTSIDE the repo, e.g.
#                               LAWPASS_ENV_PATH=/etc/lawpass/server.env
#   2. <server>/../.env.local — the consolidated single source (app/.env.local)
#   3. <server>/../.env       — fallback (legacy)
#   4. <server>/.env          — fallback (legacy server-local)
#
# Server-specific vars (already included in ../.env.example):
#   PORT=4000
#   NODE_ENV=development
#   CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000   # comma-separated; falls back to
#                                        # NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL then :3000
